{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Lesley Gore's collection feels like a natural next choice because her sixties pop connects directly with my AM Gold and older hits listening.",
    "That's Christmas To Me fits my recent choice of A Very Special Christmas and my current interest in seasonal listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The country selections miss my current mood: a hits collection alone does not make Shania Twain or Blake Shelton feel connected to the older pop and rock I have been choosing.",
    "Adele's 21 does not fit my desire for familiar older hits today, while Greatest Hits and Gold leave me unsure whose music I would be choosing."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in greatest-hits collections seems to have been taken as interest in collections by almost any artist.",
    "My occasional newer pop listening seems to have been stretched into a broader interest in contemporary music than my choices support right now."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection between AM Gold, Simon & Garfunkel, Melanie, and familiar older pop and rock matters more to me than a shared compilation title.",
    "My recent Christmas album choice gives me a specific reason to try more holiday music, without implying that my broader musical preferences have changed."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You recognized my interest in collections and holiday listening, but gave too little weight to the era and musical familiarity that make those choices appealing to me."
}"}
